    <h2 class="sg-section-title">Background</h2>
    <div class="sg-content">
      <p>Hi, I’m Sid. I study mechanical engineering and math at NC State, and I’m happiest moving between CAD, code, and a workbench. My projects have taken me from competition robots to underwater simulations, muddy rover tests, and lab automation. I’ve also researched how to shuffle a deck of cards, which turned out to involve a lot more math than you might expect.</p>
	  <br>
	  <p>A lot of how I work comes from FIRST robotics with the Zebracorns at NCSSM: building with teammates, mentoring newer students, and sharing designs other teams could use. Seeing my bumper design reach beyond our team was especially rewarding. More recently, working at iOrganBio reminded me how much I enjoy making hardware and software useful to the people who actually use them.</p>
	  <br>
	  <p>Away from the workbench, I’ve played tennis for over a decade and captained my team at NCSSM. I’m also into power sports, cars, and racing. Apparently, even my downtime tends to involve something moving quickly.</p>
	</div>

